# Day 6 (Wednesday, June 5, 1996): he wiped the computer down to Notepad, MS-DOS Prompt and
# Inbox, and left it at the shop. He deleted programs, not data.
set wallpaper: none
set desktop_color: Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
set installed_apps: PackedStringArray("Notepad")
set recently_opened: PackedStringArray("C:\\NEWSLTR\\BUILDS.TXT")
delete Desktop\Netscape Navigator
delete Desktop\mIRC32
delete Desktop\Microsoft Word
delete Desktop\Microsoft Excel
delete Desktop\Calculator.exe
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\mIRC32
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Microsoft Word
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Microsoft Excel
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Microsoft PowerPoint
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\Games
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\Multimedia
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\System Tools
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\Calculator
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\Paint
delete C:\WINDOWS\Start Menu\Programs\Accessories\WordPad
delete C:\MIRC\MIRC32.EXE
delete C:\MIRC\MIRC.INI
delete C:\Program Files\Netscape
delete C:\Program Files\Microsoft Office
delete C:\WINDOWS\CALC.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\SOL.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\PBRUSH.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\WORDPAD.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\MPLAYER.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\DEFRAG.EXE
delete C:\WINDOWS\SNDVOL32.EXE

file Desktop\MS-DOS Prompt
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons_extracted/ms_dos_window_32.png
	target: C:\WINDOWS\COMMAND.COM

file C:\NEWSLTR\BUILDS.TXT
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	modified: Tuesday, June 4, 1996 11:58:12 PM
	contents:
		BUILD NUMBERS SEEN
		updated 06/04/96

		ver         machine                    how it got there
		----------  -------------------------  -----------------------------------
		4.00.950    mine                       retail, hologram. installed 10/21/95
		4.00.950    library, front desk        retail
		4.00.950    tarnhelm                   retail
		4.00.1111   tarnhelm's work            OEM, came on the machine
		4.06.6612   fl0ppyjoe's cousin         floppies, swap meet, $5 a set
		4.06.6612   quill's shop, a customer   13 floppies, "update" and a number
		4.06.6612   3rd town (#oddbuilds)      owner doesn't remember installing it
		4.06.6612   fl0ppyjoe cousin's school  "half the school". 7 confirmed
		4.06.6612   Harlow, dentist's office   receptionist's nephew "updated" it
		4.06.6612   Millbrook, video store     staff can't remember
		4.06.6612   quill's own machine        copied calc.exe off a 6612. 06/02
		4.06.6612   tarnhelm's sister          never installed anything. 06/04
		4.06.6612   ???                        14 that i know of. stopped counting

		THE 1.4 (from quill, 06/01)
		- one cab file. quill had never seen it on a retail disk before.
		- quill found it in SETUP.INF, listed like part of windows:

		    CAMBION.CAB

		- quill listed what's inside with extract /d. he didn't extract it.
		- i haven't seen it myself, and i'm not going to.
		- a set came off the ad 06/03. didn't open it. incinerator at the dump.

		SPREAD
		- 05/30: 3 machines. 06/04: 14.
		- machines that never saw the floppies show 6612 now.
		- so it copies itself. floppies first. after that, i don't know how.

		QUILL
		- 06/02: his calc says 666.
		- 06/03: his mail bounces. user unknown.
		- 06/04: tarnhelm hasn't heard from him either.

		- wiping this box tomorrow. bare minimum. then i'm gone.

file C:\MIRC\#oddbuilds.log
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	modified: Tuesday, June 4, 1996 11:53:40 PM
	contents:
		[22:58] *** Now talking in #oddbuilds
		[22:58] *** Topic is 'post your build numbers. no warez.'
		[23:01] <elmroot> anyone else seen 4.06.6612?
		[23:01] <tarnhelm> 4.00.950 here. 4.00.1111 if you know someone at an OEM
		[23:02] <elmroot> 4.06. System Properties says so. Microsoft never made a 4.06
		[23:02] <tarnhelm> someone edited the registry for a joke
		[23:03] <elmroot> three machines now, three towns. none of the owners remember installing it
		[23:04] <quill> a guy brought one in at work. said a friend gave him floppies
		[23:04] <quill> 13 disks, labelled by hand, no hologram
		[23:05] <elmroot> what did the labels say
		[23:05] <quill> "update" and a number
		[23:06] <tarnhelm> so it's a pirate copy with a fake version
		[23:07] <elmroot> pirates don't invent build numbers. and setup is 1.4 megs bigger than retail
		[23:08] <quill> what's in the extra 1.4
		[23:08] <elmroot> working on it
		[23:12] *** tarnhelm has quit IRC (Leaving)

		[01:14] *** Now talking in #oddbuilds
		[01:15] <quill> elmroot. the 6612 guy came back. his calculator says 666
		[01:15] <elmroot> for what sum
		[01:15] <quill> any sum. 2+2. 666
		[01:16] <quill> calc on a normal build is fine. same size. different date
		[01:17] <elmroot> don't copy anything off it. don't put your own disks in it
		[01:17] <quill> too late. i copied calc.exe to look at it
		[01:18] <elmroot> then throw that floppy away
		[01:19] <quill> you sound like my mom
		[01:20] <elmroot> i mean it

		[23:40] *** Now talking in #oddbuilds
		[23:40] *** Topic is 'post your build numbers. no warez.'
		[23:41] <tarnhelm> elmroot. you there
		[23:44] <elmroot> here
		[23:44] <tarnhelm> my sister's machine says 4.06 now
		[23:45] <tarnhelm> she never installed anything. she doesn't know what a floppy is
		[23:45] <elmroot> unplug it
		[23:46] <tarnhelm> that's it? unplug it?
		[23:46] <elmroot> heard from quill?
		[23:47] <tarnhelm> no. his mail bounces
		[23:47] <elmroot> mine too
		[23:48] <tarnhelm> ok. what is it
		[23:49] <elmroot> it has a name. not saying it on irc
		[23:50] <tarnhelm> that's not an answer
		[23:51] <elmroot> i'm leaving town tomorrow
		[23:51] <tarnhelm> because of a windows version
		[23:52] <elmroot> because quill looked at it. now quill's gone
		[23:53] *** elmroot has quit IRC (going analog)

file Recycled\FOR THE SHOP.TXT
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	modified: Wednesday, June 5, 1996 8:31:05 AM
	contents:
		For whoever at the shop ends up with this box.

		I wiped what I could. My notes are in C:\NEWSLTR. Read them, then
		stop reading.

		Right-click My Computer, Properties. If it ever says 4.06, pull the
		plug and don't plug it back in. Don't put floppies from customers in
		it. Don't put its floppies in anything else.

		If you ever find that cab, don't open it. quill did.

		You fixed my RAM. Consider us even.

		- C

mail
	from: quill <quill@riverlink.net>
	to: anon654@aol.com
	subject: found your 1.4
	sent: 1996-06-01 01:47
	read: true
	body:
		the 6612 guy left his floppies at the shop. couldn't help it.

		the extra 1.4 is one cab file that i've never seen on a retail disk before. setup.inf lists it like it's part of windows:

		CAMBION.CAB

		i listed it with extract /d. i didn't extract anything, and i didn't run anything. you can stop calling me mom.

		whatever it is, it's not a typo.

mail
	from: quill <quill@riverlink.net>
	to: anon654@aol.com
	subject: calc
	sent: 1996-06-02 23:12
	read: true
	body:
		calc says 666 on my machine now. 2+2. 7*3. 666.

		my machine said 4.00.950 on friday. it says 4.06 tonight. i didn't install anything. all i did was copy calc.exe and list that cab. i never ran anything.

		you were right. throwing the floppy away didn't help.

		what do i do

mail
	from: anon654@aol.com
	to: quill <quill@riverlink.net>
	subject: Re: calc
	sent: 1996-06-03 21:30
	folder: sent
	read: true
	body:
		Unplug it. Don't boot it again. Don't copy anything off it.

		Call me on the phone, not here.

		> what do i do

