mail
	from: anon654@aol.com
	to: Kev <DoomKev@aol.com>
	subject: your mom's computer
	sent: 1996-06-05 08:02
	folder: sent
	read: true
	body:
		Kev,

		Right-click My Computer and pick Properties. If it says 4.06 anywhere, unplug it. Don't put any floppies in it, and don't take any from friends. Don't ask why.

		I'm going away for a while. Tell your mom I'll write. On paper.

		And no, you still can't borrow mine.

		Uncle Craig

mail
	from: anon654@aol.com
	to: Marge <marge.h@aol.com>
	subject: I'm out
	sent: 1996-06-05 08:15
	folder: sent
	read: true
	body:
		Marge,

		I'm leaving town today. Someone else has to take the meeting on June 12. You know the park better than I do anyway.

		Count the signatures on paper. Don't put them in a computer.

		Craig
